## `01` &nbsp;Overview

**Reliance Trends Analytics Dashboard** is an end-to-end Excel BI project built on a
**20,560-row retail sales fact table**, modelled against four supporting dimension
tables (Customers, Products, Stores, Inventory). It turns raw transactional data into
an **interactive, single-screen dashboard** with charts, KPIs, and drill-downs across
country, department, city, season and time.

> Built entirely with native Excel — PivotTables, PivotCharts, formulas and slicers.
> No Power BI, no external add-ins.

<img width="100%" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/andreasbm/readme/master/assets/lines/rainbow.png" alt="divider" />

## `02` &nbsp;Key Metrics

| Metric | Value |
| :--- | :--- |
| Total Sales | ₹594.5 Cr (`5,945,445,219`) |
| Total Gross Profit | ₹225.2 Cr (`2,252,425,901`) |
| Units Sold | `37,310` |
| Transactions | `20,560` |
| Countries Covered | 7 — India, UAE, USA, UK, Singapore, Russia, South Africa |
| Departments | Accessories · Kidswear · Menswear · Womenswear |
| Stores | `82` across 7 countries |
| Customers | `4,030` |
| Products (SKUs) | `481` |
| Years | 2025 – 2026 |

<img width="100%" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/andreasbm/readme/master/assets/lines/rainbow.png" alt="divider" />

## `03` &nbsp;Workbook Structure

<table>
<tr><th>Sheet</th><th>Rows</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>dashboard</code></td><td>—</td><td>Interactive summary view — 8 charts, KPI cards, country/segment breakdowns</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>pivot tables</code></td><td>—</td><td>PivotTables: profit by country, sales by year/month, top customers, item-level sales, membership tiers, manager/store counts, city-wise profit by state</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>sales values</code></td><td>—</td><td>Department, city, and country roll-ups; YoY profit-margin comparison</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Sales_data</code></td><td>20,560</td><td>Core transactional fact table — order, product, customer, store, pricing and return details (48 columns)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Customers</code></td><td>4,030</td><td>Customer dimension — demographics, segment, membership tier</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Products</code></td><td>481</td><td>Product dimension — category, brand, size, color, material, season</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Stores</code></td><td>82</td><td>Store dimension — location, format, manager, region</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Inventory</code></td><td>4,000</td><td>Stock levels and inventory status by product/store</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>formulas</code></td><td>17</td><td>Reference sheet mapping business questions to the exact formula used</td></tr>
</table>

<img width="100%" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/andreasbm/readme/master/assets/lines/rainbow.png" alt="divider" />

## `04` &nbsp;Dashboard Highlights

- **Gross profit by country** — horizontal bar chart, India leading at ₹98.9 Cr
- **Top 5 customers by profit** — ranked line/bar view
- **Sales & profit by department** — Accessories, Kidswear, Menswear, Womenswear
- **Season-wise sales** — All Season, Monsoon, Summer, Winter split by department
- **City-wise profit** — UK & US city breakdown with grand totals
- **Membership tier distribution** — Gold / Platinum / Silver by country
- **Store & manager counts** — operational footprint per country
- **YoY profit margin** — 2025 vs 2026 by country

<img width="100%" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/andreasbm/readme/master/assets/lines/rainbow.png" alt="divider" />

## `05` &nbsp;Formulas Used

The `formulas` sheet documents every business question against its exact Excel
formula — a quick-reference for the logic behind the dashboard:

`SUM` · `AVERAGE` · `MAX` · `MIN` · `COUNT` · `SUMIF` · `COUNTIF` · `AVERAGEIF` ·
`SUMIFS` · `COUNTIFS` · `MAXIFS` · `MINIFS` · `IF`

```text
Total Sales     =SUM(Sales_data!AG:AG)
India Sales     =SUMIF(Sales_data!K:K,"india",Sales_data!AG:AG)
India Sales '26 =SUMIFS(Sales_data!AG:AG,Sales_data!D:D,"2026",Sales_data!K:K,"india")
Is Profitable?  =IF(Sales_data!AJ2=0,0,"profitable")
```

<img width="100%" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/andreasbm/readme/master/assets/lines/rainbow.png" alt="divider" />

